@file fixtures/txf.nw
@begin docs 0
@end docs 0
@begin docs 1
@text # Float transclusion fixture
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text A Markdown document that exercises the float node model (§10). A labelled figure
@nl
@text and a labelled equation live inside a section. A later section refers to each and
@nl
@text transcludes each. So the weave must lift one element out of a section body, give
@nl
@text it a node page of its own, and inline it where the directive sits.
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text ## The originals {#sec:home}
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text Here are the floats the rest of the document points at: the figure \ref{fig:demo}
@nl
@text and the relation \ref{eq:demo}.
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text ```math \label{eq:demo}
@nl
@text E = mc^2
@nl
@text ```
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text ```figure \label{fig:demo}
@nl
@text \caption{A *tiny* schematic.}
@nl
@text <img src="demo.svg" alt="a demo">
@nl
@text ```
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text ## The reuse {#sec:reuse}
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text The figure appears again here, lifted out on its own:
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text \transclude{fig:demo}
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text And the equation too:
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text \transclude{eq:demo}
@nl
@end docs 1
